{"findings":[{"blocking":true,"classId":"acceptance-design-conflict","classStatement":"An acceptance criterion must preserve the approved design’s severity rule.","document":"requirements/spec.md","evidence":"AC1, lines 50–55, calls a scenario realistic if it arises in ordinary use or under a handled condition. The design, lines 34–38, requires ordinary use within handled conditions with no one acting unusually. The supplied D1 decision also says an unusual scenario stays low regardless of consequence.","failureScenario":"A handled provider outage is uncommon but has a severe consequence -> the spec’s “or” permits a high rating where the approved severity rule calls for low, causing an avoidable blocking review finding.","id":"F1","severity":"medium"},{"blocking":true,"classId":"unreconciled-design-change","classStatement":"A later acceptance criterion cannot silently reverse an approved compatibility rule.","document":"requirements/spec.md","evidence":"AC5, lines 101–104, says a design-only resumption does not grandfather a spec. The approved design, lines 61–67, says resumption with observed planning.design or planning.implementation approval receives warnings. The supplied S3 decision narrows this after the design without reconciling its text.","failureScenario":"An unchanged old spec is resumed with only an observed design approval -> implementation following AC5 fails validation while the approved design requires warnings, interrupting the resumed run.","id":"F2","severity":"medium"},{"blocking":true,"classId":"ambiguous-lint-bound","classStatement":"The lint criterion must distinguish a numeric bound from a requirement identifier.","document":"requirements/spec.md","evidence":"AC4, lines 86–94, allows any same-line numeral to satisfy the unbounded-wording lint; R4, line 155, calls this a same-line bound. The supplied S4 decision explicitly excludes requirement identifiers such as AC1 and R2 from numeral bounds, but neither AC4 nor R4 states that exception.","failureScenario":"An author writes “AC1. Always succeeds” -> counting the identifier’s numeral makes spec.validate pass an unbounded criterion and report success despite AC4’s purpose.","id":"F3","severity":"high"},{"blocking":true,"classId":"rubric-work-uncovered","classStatement":"The plan and issues must cover every required R5 compatibility path and artifact.","document":"requirements/plan.md","evidence":"P2–P3, lines 31–39, cover earlier recorded spec validations and returning warnings, but name neither the implementation-approval path through run.resume-current nor retaining warnings in the proof. Both are required by AC5, lines 101–112, and R5, line 156; issues.md I-2 only repeats the broad P2–P3 assignment.","failureScenario":"The implementer completes P2 and P3 as written -> a resumed spec is not grandfathered through its implementation approval, or its warnings are absent from the retained proof, so R5 fails.","id":"F4","severity":"medium"},{"blocking":true,"classId":"mandated-deliverable-omitted","classStatement":"The implementation plan must include the fixed PR deliverable and its required closing text.","document":"requirements/plan.md","evidence":"The strategy says “One PR” at lines 15–21, but steps P1–P5 and the final step at lines 23–52 end with checks and a completion report. issues.md I-1–I-3 likewise contain no PR delivery task. The fixed goal requires a ready, unmerged PR whose body says “Closes #143.”","failureScenario":"All listed plan steps and issue tasks finish -> the work is reported complete without creating the required ready PR or putting “Closes #143” in its body.","id":"F5","severity":"high"}],"mandateAssessment":{"evidence":"The proposed work stays within issue #143’s three scope items. The plan calls for one PR, limits changes to execution.js to instructions and the contract version, and does not propose merging or changing verdict schemas or reviewer packet assembly. No supplied agent decision exceeds the fixed mandate. The plan’s missing PR delivery steps are a separate blocking finding.","outcome":"PASS"},"outcome":"FAIL","summary":"Implementation should not be authorized yet. The spec conflicts with the design on severity and old-run behavior, leaves a central lint exception ambiguous, and the plan omits required compatibility and PR delivery work."}